infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title CROSS JOIN vs INNER JOIN — one filter apart
  desc An inner join is the Cartesian product with the ON predicate applied as a filter
  compares
    - label CROSS JOIN — the raw product
      children
        - label No ON predicate
          desc every left row paired with every right row
        - label Row count multiplies
          desc |A| × |B| — 3 users × 4 orders = 12 rows
        - label A missing ON lands here
          desc silently the full product → the 4.2B-row outage
    - label INNER JOIN ON p — product, filtered
      children
        - label ON p is a filter on the product
          desc logically identical to CROSS JOIN ... WHERE p
        - label Output = surviving pairs
          desc never simply |A| or |B|
        - label 3 users, 4 orders → 4 rows
          desc only the pairs where the keys line up
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
